Subject: [PATCH] d2d1: cap split count in d2d_geometry_resolve_beziers

d2d_geometry_resolve_beziers runs an outer overlap-then-split loop:

    while (d2d_geometry_check_bezier_overlap(p, q))
        d2d_geometry_split_bezier(p or q)

For pathological geometries (overlapping/collinear beziers in SVG
imports), the overlap check stays true after each split because float
precision prevents the control-triangle area from shrinking enough.
The loop never terminates and Affinity hangs on double-click of
imported vector groups.

Wrap d2d_geometry_split_bezier with a thread-local counter (max 512
splits per resolve). Once the budget is exhausted split_bezier returns
FALSE which the caller already handles by aborting the resolve. The
counter is reset at the entry of d2d_geometry_resolve_beziers.

Mirrors the WineFix BezierSplitBudgetPatch (NativeHook on Wine 9.13
d2d1.dll), but applied at source level so it works on the Wine 10.18
standalone build shipped with affinity-nix.

--- a/src/geometry.c	2026-05-18 10:43:49.692616710 +0200
+++ b/src/geometry.c	2026-05-18 10:44:31.063379277 +0200
@@ -3336,8 +3336,17 @@
             &figure->bezier_controls[idx->control_idx], &figure->vertices[next]);
 }
 
+/* Thread-local cap to prevent unbounded splitting in d2d_geometry_resolve_beziers
+ * when pathological geometries (overlapping/collinear beziers) make
+ * d2d_geometry_check_bezier_overlap loop forever. Reset at the start of
+ * d2d_geometry_resolve_beziers. */
+static __thread int d2d_split_budget = 0;
+
 static BOOL d2d_geometry_split_bezier(struct d2d_geometry *geometry, const struct d2d_segment_idx *idx)
 {
+    if (++d2d_split_budget > 512)
+        return FALSE;
+
     const D2D1_POINT_2F *p[3];
     struct d2d_figure *figure;
     D2D1_POINT_2F q[3];
@@ -3371,6 +3380,8 @@
     struct d2d_figure *figure;
     size_t bezier_idx, i;
 
+    d2d_split_budget = 0;
+
     if (!d2d_geometry_get_first_bezier_segment_idx(geometry, &idx_p))
         return S_OK;
 
